WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.210
It's no secret that Netflix is a big spender.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:08.870
In 2017 alone, the streaming service dropped
$6.3 billion on original and acquired programming

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:15.000
- demolishing the video content budgets of
Viacom, Amazon, CBS, Apple, and Facebook.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.730
But the lion's share of Netflix's budget,
of course, goes to original programming.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.070
And to do that, the company has signed off
on some seriously extravagant series.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.460
But which are the most expensive shows Netflix
has ever produced?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.640
We've got your numbers.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.999
Hemlock Grove

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:35.680
American creature-killer series Hemlock Grove
was supposed to be a surefire hit for Netflix.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.430
But it ended up being little more than an
average show with a hefty price tag.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.070
"Is there something you wanna tell me?"

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.890
"I'm about to do things I don't want to.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.670
But sooner or later I'm gonna have to give
in."

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:51.970
When it premiered in 2013, Hemlock Grove ranked
among Netflix's most expensive shows to date,

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:57.400
reportedly costing $40 million for Season
One's 13 episodes - far more than most major

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.030
television networks are willing to shell out
for even a 22-episode run.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.180
"Your entire bloodline's about to become extinct."

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:08.700
The series received a less-than-stellar critical
reception, though it did manage to garner

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.759
a dedicated fan-base which ultimately kept
the show alive for two additional seasons

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:15.560
before Netflix pulled the plug.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.219
Orange is the New Black

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:21.850
As one of Netflix's most well-known and widely
acclaimed series, it's not surprising that

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.700
Orange Is the New Black ranks among the most
expensive offerings on the platform.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.710
"These are complicated ladies in a complicated
place."

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.909
According to Peter Micelli, former co-head
of TV at CAA, the show runs just under $4

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:35.689
million per episode.

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:40.229
But investing in the screen rights to Piper
Kerman's memoir of the same name has paid

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:45.070
massive dividends for Netflix - in awards,
and worldwide brand recognition.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.380
"We're gonna be super famous.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.029
Don't forget to smeyes."

00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:52.270
House of Cards

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:57.329
At the time of its creation, political thriller
House of Cards set a new standard for Netflix

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:00.590
- for quality, as well as production costs.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.930
Former star and executive producer Kevin Spacey
once said production reportedly spent $100

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.080
million on the first season alone.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.310
"We don't submit to terror.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.660
We make the terror."

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.970
As the show closes in on its sixth and final
season, sans Spacey, in late 2018 - the series

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.750
will go down as a hit for the platform.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:25.300
Netflix reportedly upped their subscriber
count by at least 27.5 million when House

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:31.050
of Cards debuted in 2013 - with the ultra-popular
political drama playing a major role in the

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.280
streaming service winning their fans' vote.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.670
"We're just getting started."

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.340
Seinfeld's comedy

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.000
Netflix isn't just shelling out for high-profile
original series.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.830
It's also forking it over for original stand-up,
as well.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.790
And no deal was more expensive than the one
they made with Jerry Seinfeld.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.120
"Would I have been funny if I grew up in Peoria
in a whorehouse, raised by prostitutes?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.120
Absolutely.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.160
But this is what I had to work with."

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.710
Netflix reportedly paid Seinfeld a staggering
$100 million for a pair of stand-up specials,

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:05.950
bundled with the streaming rights to his hit
web series Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.120
But the platform was happy to pay Seinfeld's
lofty premium.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.030
Netflix's chief content officer, Ted Sarandos,
told Deadline,

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.860
"Jerry is known the world over as both a great
TV innovator and beloved comic voice.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.510
We are incredibly proud to welcome him to
the Netflix comedy family."

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.510
"You excited?"

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.470
"I wouldn't say I'm excited, but I'm looking
forward to it."

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.250
The Get Down

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:33.020
Baz Luhrmann and Stephen Adly Guirgis' South
Bronx musical drama, The Get Down, caused

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.380
a lot of tension between Sony Pictures Television
and Netflix.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:41.061
According to Variety, the show's two-and-a-half
year production saw two showrunners and a

00:03:41.061 --> 00:03:45.310
whole slew of writers come and go - allegedly
due to Luhrmann's involvement.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:50.730
A money-burning budget coupled with a lack
of actual filming saw Sony get fed up quickly,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.160
but Netflix's Sarandos refused to greenlight
development until Luhrmann agreed to direct

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.600
the series from start to finish.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.110
"The borough where I'm from ain't the slums.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.490
We got kings.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.050
And that's what I'll be.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.569
My friends and me."

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:07.880
When The Get Down's 12-episode season finally
wrapped, production reportedly ended up costing

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:13.960
at least $120 million - and possibly more
than $190 million, all in - making it one

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.720
of the most expensive shows in television
history.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:17.740
[scream]

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:22.920
But while it was canceled after its first
season, Netflix's VP of original content,

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.460
Cindy Holland, told Variety,

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:28.170
"We're about supporting our artists and supporting
their vision.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:33.320
Working with Baz and his team was one of the
most rewarding experiences of my life."

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.320
The Crown

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.020
Netflix's historical drama The Crown tells
the biographical story of Queen Elizabeth

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.690
II - and boasts production costs that would
make the real royal family tighten their corsets.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.150
"What do you want, a degree?

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.620
No one wants a college lecturer as sovereign.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.820
They want a queen."

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:54.710
The show's first season alone reportedly cost
a record-setting $130 million in 2016.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.350
Although show creator Peter Morgan thinks
that estimation is closer to the total cost

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:06.460
for the first two seasons, that still equates
to a whopping $6.5 to $13 million per hour-long

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.460
episode.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:11.190
Helping drive up production costs was the
flawless recreation of Queen Elizabeth's wedding

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:14.050
dress - which cost approximately $37,000.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:20.440
"We had teams of six people working for six
weeks, just embroidering the train and the

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.440
dress."

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:25.880
That, and someone had to sign off on a life-size
replica of Buckingham Palace.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.880
Altered Carbon

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:33.610
Debuting in February 2018, dystopian cyberpunk
series Altered Carbon is rumored to be one

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:35.580
of Netflix's most expensive shows.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:41.020
"You've been provided with this body, which
came equipped with military-grade neuro-chem,

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.330
and combat muscle memory."

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.150
Based on the 2002 novel by Richard K. Morgan,
Altered Carbon remained in development for

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.510
nearly a decade and a half.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:55.350
Originally optioned by Warner Brothers, the
show began its expensive march to Netflix's

00:05:55.350 --> 00:06:00.139
lineup once Terminator Genisys screenwriter
Laeta Kalogridis - and Games of Thrones director

00:06:00.139 --> 00:06:02.500
Miguel Sapochnik - signed on.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:07.400
The exact cost of Altered Carbon's production
remains a conservatively estimated $7 million

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.420
per episode.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.150
However, Kalogridis told THR,

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.889
"That number is really funny.

00:06:11.889 --> 00:06:15.000
I feel comfortable saying that that number
is not correct.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.449
I would say it's inaccurate."

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:21.310
Regardless of how off the first season's $70
million estimate may be, if this show gets

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:26.080
its second season, it'll likely be breaking
the bank as one of Netflix's most expensive

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.080
shows ever.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.480
"I thought you'd be bigger.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.720
They made me bring all this backup."

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.220
Thanks for watching!

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.660
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.330
Plus, check out this other cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

